1
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
A father and a daughter, divided by a case, endangered by the truth.

2
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Class Action is a drama, crime, history film directed by Michael Apted.

3
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
A liberal activist lawyer alienated his daughter Maggie
years ago when she discovered his many affairs.

4
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Now a conservative corporate lawyer, Maggie agrees to
go up against her father in court.

5
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
To gain promotion, she must defend an auto manufacturer against charges
that their explosion-prone station wagons are unsafe.

6
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
As her mother begs for peace, Maggie takes on her dad in a
trial that turns increasingly personal and nasty.

7
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Jedediah Tucker Ward, played by Gene Hackman.

8
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Maggie Ward, played by Mary Elizabeth Mastrantonio.

9
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Michael Grazier, played by Colin Friels.

10
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
Estelle Ward, played by Joanna Merlin.

11
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Nick Holbrook, played by Laurence Fishburne.

12
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Quinn, played by Donald Moffat.

13
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
Class Action is a 1991 American legal drama film directed by Michael Apted.

14
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
Gene Hackman and Mary Elizabeth Mastrantonio star; Laurence Fishburne, Colin
Friels, Fred Dalton Thompson, and Donald Moffat are also featured.

15
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The film was entered into the 17th Moscow International Film Festival.

16
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The film explores themes of lawyer, courtroom, auto industry,
father daughter conflict, estranged daughter.

17
